{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And he made with it.</b> From that wave-offering. <b>With it</b> in place of 'from it,' as I explained regarding מראות הצובאות." "<b>The sockets of the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.</b> From the sixty-five talents of copper they made sixty-five copper sockets for the entire court all around and for the screen of the entrance of the Mishkan — a talent per socket. And from the five remaining talents and the one thousand seven hundred (ואלפים וד׳ מאות) shekels they made the copper altar and its utensils, and the pegs of the Mishkan and the court. It is found that he omitted explaining here the copper clasps for the eleven curtains and the mallets for driving the pegs, according to what Rashi explained at the end of Parashat Terumah. But there is no wondering about the basin (כיור), as Rashi explained at the end of Parashat Vayakhel. Let it not arise in a person's heart to say that they donated gold and silver and copper only what is written here, for they donated much more than what is written here; rather, it tells you concerning the gold only what was needed for the work of gold, and the surplus they gave to the treasury for all sacred and communal needs. And so they did with the silver and with the copper. And it is impossible to say that they donated exactly to the measure of what was needed. And it is also impossible to say that he counted nineteen-year-olds and sixty-one-year-olds and seventy-year-olds and eighty-year-olds who were not in the count of six hundred thousand and did not donate — for as it is written, 'כל מרים תרומת כסף ונחשת,' which implies that whoever wishes to bring a donation may bring it, even if they are not twenty years old or older than sixty. One might say they brought only a beka per head — but surely they donated and had much left over, as it is written, 'and there was surplus (והותר).'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {1 "The text reads אלפים וד׳ מאות — literally 'thousands and four hundred,' i.e., two thousand four hundred; resolved as one thousand seven hundred based on the biblical figure in Exodus 38:28. The abbreviation חז״ק resolved as 'it is found that' (הרי שיר)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:17.549462783Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}